  "description_md": "Given a string, find the length of the longest contiguous substring that has no repeated characters.\n\n**Example:** for `\"abcabcbb\"` the longest such substring is `\"abc\"`, length 3. For `\"bbbbb\"` it's `\"b\"`, length 1. For `\"pwwkew\"` it's `\"wke\"`, length 3 (note the substring doesn't need to be a prefix).\n\n**Constraints:** string length up to ~5*10^4; may contain letters, digits, symbols, and spaces.",
  "signature": {
   "name": "lengthOfLongestSubstring",
   "params": [
    {
     "name": "s",
     "kind": "value"
    }
   ],
   "returns": {
    "kind": "value"
   }
  },
  "starter_code": "def lengthOfLongestSubstring(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    s: str\n    Returns: int\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n",
  "reference_solution": "def lengthOfLongestSubstring(s):\n    charSet = set()\n    l = 0\n    res = 0\n    for r in range(len(s)):\n        while s[r] in charSet:\n            charSet.remove(s[l])\n            l += 1\n        charSet.add(s[r])\n        res = max(res, r - l + 1)\n    return res\n",
